  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right now we can only do `SendCustomEvent` via an animation file while the animator is on the same gameObject as a UdonBehaviour. There are various ways to do this within a state, but it will still require a animation file.\nHowever, if we had a StateMachineBehaviour for SendCustomEvent (and Set Variable) we could do this without needing extra animators, and potentially not have the requirement of needing a UdonBehaviour on the same gameObject as the animator. Possibly reducing the overall UdonBehaviours in a scene depending on the creators need.\nWhether or not it will support all the state machine behaviour methods will be a design/performance choice.\nhttps://docs.unity3d.com/540/Documentation/ScriptReference/StateMachineBehaviour.html\nSendCustomEvent\n- State Method (OnStateEnter/OnStateExit/OnStateIK/OnStateMove)\n- UdonBehaviour\n- value\nSet Variable\n- State Method (OnStateEnter/OnStateExit/OnStateIK/OnStateMove)\n- UdonBehaviour\n- name\n- value\nAlternative\n- State Method (OnStateEnter/OnStateExit/OnStateIK/OnStateMove)\n- UdonBehaviour\n- Type (Send Event / Set Variable)\n- Name? (Set Variable)\n- Value\nThese are just examples, and will not reflect on how or if VRC will implement it.",
